{"duration": 48.643, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A captain kept his ship anchored offshore, desperate to reach the city.", "start": 0.05, "end": 2.751}, {"beat": 0, "text": "Venice was close, but his crew could not step ashore.", "start": 2.831, "end": 5.18}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Between 1348 and 1359, the Black Death wiped out an estimated 30% of Europe's population.", "start": 5.38, "end": 10.838}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Venice's trade depended on fleets of three thousand three hundred ships.", "start": 10.918, "end": 13.855}, {"beat": 2, "text": "In 1377, Ragusa made every newcomer wait thirty days on nearby islands.", "start": 14.055, "end": 18.139}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The captain watched for signs of the plague before anyone could land.", "start": 18.219, "end": 20.895}, {"beat": 3, "text": "In 1448, the Venetian Senate stretched that wait to forty days.", "start": 21.095, "end": 24.329}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Dubrovnik built the Lazzarettos, Europe's first quarantine sites.", "start": 24.409, "end": 27.145}, {"beat": 3, "text": "The word for that wait was quarantena: forty days.", "start": 27.225, "end": 29.472}, {"beat": 4, "text": "You see, the wait was like waiting out a cough before hugging your family.", "start": 29.672, "end": 32.467}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Current estimates put the bubonic plague at thirty-seven days from infection to death.", "start": 32.667, "end": 36.239}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Forty days outlasted the sickness, so the quarantine worked.", "start": 36.319, "end": 38.992}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Scholars also linked the forty days to Hippocrates, Lent, and alchemy's philosophical month.", "start": 39.072, "end": 43.296}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Venice gave the world the word quarantine.", "start": 43.496, "end": 45.244}, {"beat": 6, "text": "But Ragusa began the practice first, with thirty days.", "start": 45.324, "end": 47.743}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.09, "end": 0.115, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "cap